  "chapter": {
    "number": 108,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(109) For the end, a Psalm of David."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For the end, a Psalm of David. O God, pass not over my praise in silence;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "for the mouth of the sinner and the mouth of the crafty man have been opened against me: they have spoken against me with a crafty tongue.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And they have compassed me with words of hatred; and fought against me without a cause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "noteId": 206
          },
          {
            "text": "Instead of loving me, they falsely accused me: but I continued to pray.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And they rewarded me evil for good, and hatred for my love.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Set you a sinner against him; and let",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 207
          },
          {
            "text": "the devil stand at his right hand.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "When he is judged, let him go forth condemned: and let his prayer become sin.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let his days be few: and let another take his office of overseer.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let his children be orphans, and his wife a widow.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let his children wander without a dwelling-place, and beg: let them be cast out of their habitations.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let his creditor exact all that belongs to him: and let strangers spoil his labors.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let him have no helper; neither let there be any one to have compassion on his fatherless children.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let his children be given up to utter destruction: in one generation let his name be blotted out.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let the iniquity of his fathers be remembered before the Lord; and let not the sin of his mother be blotted out.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 15,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let them be before the Lord continually; and let their memorial be blotted out from the earth.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 16,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Because he remembered not to show mercy, but persecuted the needy and poor man, and that to kill him that was pricked in the heart.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 17,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He loved cursing also, and it shall come upon him; and he took not pleasure in blessing, so it shall be removed far from him.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 18,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Yes, he put on cursing as a garment, and it is come as water into his bowels, and as oil into his bones.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 19,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let it be to him as a garment which he puts on, and as a girdle with which he girds himself continually.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 20,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "This is the dealing of the Lord with those who falsely accuse me, and of them that speak evil against my soul.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 21,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But you, O Lord, Lord, deal mercifully with me, for your name's sake: for your mercy is good.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 22,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Deliver me, for I am poor and needy; and my heart is troubled within me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 23,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I am removed as a shadow in its going down: I am tossed up and down like locusts.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 24,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "My knees are weakened through fasting, and my flesh is changed by reason of the lack of oil.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 25,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I became also a reproach to them: when they saw me they shook their heads.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 26,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Help me, O Lord my God; and save me according to your mercy.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 27,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And let them know that this is your hand; and that you, Lord, have wrought it.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 28,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let them curse, but you shall bless: let them that rise up against me be ashamed, but let your servant rejoice.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 29,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let those that falsely accuse me be clothed with shame, and let them cover themselves with their shame as with a mantle.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 30,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I will give thanks to the Lord abundantly with my mouth; and in the midst of many I will praise him.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 31,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For he stood on the right hand of the poor, to save me from them that persecute my soul.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 206,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Or, in return for my love.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 108,
          "verse": 4
        }
      },
      {
        "noteId": 207,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Or, the accuser.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 108,
          "verse": 6
        }
      }
    ]
  },
